  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ukrainian Women Entrepreneurs Hub II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ukrainian women entrepreneurs face gender-based barriers and lack the necessary knowledge and practical skills in business planning in a modern business environment. That is due to generally inadequate entrepreneurship and business education in Ukraine, which focuses on theory-oriented instead of skills-oriented, and gender-based barriers, like discrimination, in a male-dominated business environment.  Moreover, during the war, the role of women has changed. Since many men serve in the army, women have become those who are now of the Ukrainian economy. At the same time, the number of obligations for women has increased - to provide for the family, take care of children, and develop themselves to cope with all this. In addition, the war itself causes psychological stress. Ukrainian women are to develop themselves in business skills and coping strategies for the war. The specific training needs and other support depend very much on the local situation. Three locations are chosen. These locations are Irpin and Borodyanka (Kyiv region), both liberated and Poltava, where many refugees settled.The ambition of CSR Ukraine is to have a network of service centres for female business owners and managers that are business-oriented and supportive. Ukraine itself has little tradition in developing business. Therefore, CSR Ukraine needs a partner with the necessary skills for this.</narrative>
  </description>
